{"id": "89048645-4c7c-460d-ba59-89cf066bff02", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Cross-region Identity Center setups are actually supported for Amazon Q Business — the org-level IAM Identity Center instance doesn't have to live in the same region as the Q Business app, so that mismatch by itself usually isn't the blocker. But let me verify that and trace the actual authorization chain for your app rather than guess, since a ChatSync failure for users could come from several different hops (trust policy, Identity Center application assignment, SCPs, etc.).

Let me dig into your Q Business app's configuration and the surrounding IAM/Identity Center setup.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_TtQ510MXszAXJjp28cbwO9", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Diagnose why users cannot chat with an Amazon Q Business application. The customer has an org-level IAM Identity Center instance in us-west-2, while the Q Business application is in us-east-1, and suspects this cross-region setup is the cause.",
  "context": "User wants a root-cause diagnosis of a Q Business chat failure (likely ChatSync access-denied or identity-resolution failure). Before concluding the cross-region Identity Center hypothesis is correct, verify via AWS documentation whether Q Business requires the IAM Identity Center instance to be in the same region as the application, or whether an org-level instance in a different region is a supported configuration. Then trace the actual authorization chain for this specific app to find the real failure point.",
  "resources": ["Amazon Q Business application(s) in us-east-1", "IAM Identity Center organization instance in us-west-2", "IAM roles/trust policies associated with the Q Business app and its index/retriever", "SCPs if applicable"],
  "approach": "Read and follow the aiml-access-diagnostics skill for methodology (trace caller identity, iam:PassRole, trust policy, role permissions, resource policies, SCPs to name the exact denying hop). Use verify_aws_claim to confirm or refute the cross-region Identity Center hypothesis against published AWS documentation. Use use_aws (read-only describe/list/get calls) to inspect the actual Q Business app config, its identity center application ARN/instance ARN, and associated IAM roles.",
  "criteria": "Determine: (1) whether cross-region Identity Center is actually a valid supported config per AWS docs, (2) the Q Business app's current identity-center instance ARN and region, (3) whether the Identity Center instance attached to the app matches expectations, (4) the specific hop (if any) causing chat/ChatSync failures — e.g. missing Identity Center application assignment, trust policy misconfiguration, missing permissions, or something unrelated to region at all.",
  "aws_account_id": "012345678901_2",
  "aws_regions": ["us-east-1", "us-west-2"]
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Diagnose Q Business chat failure, checking IAM/Identity Center auth chain across regions"}], "created_at": null}

